title: orbital_context
---
// The orbital station of the Science dimension (`specs/orbital_station/`):
// one node per resident. The errand of consignment 0447 (quest
// `orbital_consignment`) runs through Okafor at customs, Georg Canter in
// the Math town's Surveyor's Office (`math.yarn`), and back.
//
// Flags: `orbital_consignment_query` (Okafor asks for a signed count),
// `orbital_manifest_signed` (Canter signs it), `orbital_consignment_cleared`
// (Okafor clears the crate: the freight lane's gates open) and
// `orbital_spur_pass` (the hatch of the damaged spur opens).
//
// Never played. No placement names this node; it declares the zone.
===

title: station_okafor
---
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "orbital_consignment_cleared")>>
    Officer Okafor: Lane's open. Crate 0447 went on the Remainder at shift change.
    -> Anything else held?
        Officer Okafor: Always. Not today's problem. Hamid wanted someone in the spur; your pass is on the hatch.
    -> ⟨step away⟩
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "orbital_manifest_signed")>>
    Officer Okafor: A signature from the Math town. "Twelve lenses. Finite." He underlined finite.
    -> Clear the crate.
        <<command "world.set_flag" "orbital_consignment_cleared" true>>
        <<command "world.set_flag" "orbital_spur_pass" true>>
        Officer Okafor: Stamped. The pen opens and the lane to the bay with it. One more thing: Hamid needs someone in the damaged spur who does not breathe. I put a pass on the hatch.
    -> Not yet.
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "orbital_consignment_query")>>
    Officer Okafor: Still need a count I can stamp. Surveyor's Office, Math town. Ask for Canter.
    -> Where is the Math town?
        Officer Okafor: Through the ring and up the stairs from its gate hall. The office is on the second terrace.
    -> ⟨step away⟩
<<else>>
    Officer Okafor: Customs. Crate 0447 in my pen is survey lenses from the Math town, for the Remainder. The manifest gives the count as "aleph-null". I cannot clear an infinite crate.
    -> I can ask the sender.
        <<command "world.set_flag" "orbital_consignment_query" true>>
        Officer Okafor: Surveyor's Office, Math town. Bring me a number I can stamp.
    -> Why so careful?
        Officer Okafor: Seed stock, spores, mail with ideas in it. The ring moves anything. Somebody has to look first.
    -> ⟨step away⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: station_reyes
---
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "orbital_consignment_cleared")>>
    Captain Reyes: 0447 is aboard. We burn for the survey moon at shift change. Thanks for fetching a number.
    -> Why does the moon need lenses?
        Captain Reyes: To map it. Then someone will want a ring there, and I will be out of work. Good.
    -> ⟨step away⟩
<<else>>
    Captain Reyes: That pen on the gate deck holds my lenses. Without them the survey is blind.
    -> What do you haul?
        Captain Reyes: Whatever the ring brings that has to go where no ring is. Moons, mines, the slow places.
    -> Why not put a ring on the moon?
        Captain Reyes: A ring eats a reactor and a crew. A hauler eats patience. Patience is cheaper.
    -> ⟨step away⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: station_lindqvist
---
Bo Lindqvist: Ring throughput is down a third since they doubled the passenger slots. Freight waits. I wait.
-> Why passengers first?
    Bo Lindqvist: They complain louder than crates. Also they get sick in the ring, so they want it over fast.
-> Need a hand?
    Bo Lindqvist: Not unless you can lift a container. ...You can? Huh. Union says no.
-> ⟨step away⟩
===

title: station_rahimi
---
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "switch_orbital_spur_breaker_used")>>
    Hamid Rahimi: Power is back in the spur. The crawlers went quiet when the breaker closed. I owe you.
    -> What broke them?
        Hamid Rahimi: Their orders. "Repair anything damaged." The storm damaged everything. They kept cutting.
    -> ⟨step away⟩
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "orbital_spur_pass")>>
    Hamid Rahimi: Okafor logged your pass. The spur took a storm last cycle. Breaker's tripped at the far end.
    -> What is in there?
        Hamid Rahimi: No air, live cable under the deck, and maintenance crawlers that do not stop. Reset the breaker if you can.
    -> ⟨step away⟩
<<else>>
    Hamid Rahimi: Service deck. Don't touch anything that hums.
    -> What is behind the hatch?
        Hamid Rahimi: The old spur. Damaged. Shut until customs signs off on someone with a pass and no lungs.
    -> How much power does the ring take?
        Hamid Rahimi: Opening it, all of it. Holding it, half. That is why we schedule.
    -> ⟨step away⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: station_pell
---
Gus Pell: First time through the ring? People come up those stairs green. Crackers by the door.
-> I don't get sick.
    Gus Pell: A robot. Lucky. Some folks lose a day to it. Some just lose breakfast.
-> What's cooking?
    Gus Pell: Greens from the racks, and whatever came through the gate this morning. Today, beans.
-> ⟨step away⟩
===

title: station_wen
---
Wen Liang: I tuned this station's first stable ring. The first link held three seconds. Now people commute.
-> What changed?
    Wen Liang: Power got cheap. Everybody wants a gate now. Not everybody wants to pay for one.
-> Do you miss the work?
    Wen Liang: I miss the quiet. Look down instead. That never gets old.
-> ⟨step away⟩
===

title: station_neil
---
Neil onGras Turfson: Well, actually, that blue line on the edge is all the air they have. Thinner than paint on a ball.
-> It looks fragile.
    Neil onGras Turfson: It is. Look at it long enough and you will want to go down and touch some grass.
-> ⟨step away⟩
===
